    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60846" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῠνηγ-έω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῠνηγ-ᾱγέω</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Bion
			1.60
		</span></i>: pf.
		
			Pass.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκυνηγῆσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					31.29.4
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυνηγός</span>):—<i>hunt,
				chase</i>, later form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυνηγετέω,
				ὅταν κυνηγήσῃ [ὁ ἀετός</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				619a33
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pel.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, etc.: metaph., <i>pursue, persecute</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				349c
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
